                <pb facs="0911" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1989-92v31/pg884"/>


                <head>Paper Prepared in the Department of State<anchor n="58" xml:id="d161-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian">undated</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Agreed Statement</hi></p>
                <p>The Parties agree that, with regard to paragraph 5 of Article II of the Treaty,
                    the requirement that the strategic offensive arms of each Party shall be based
                    only within its national territory refers to permanent basing involving the
                    establishment of facilities equipped to support <pb facs="0912" n="885"
                        xml:id="pg885"/> the long-term operation of strategic offensive arms. The
                    obligations of paragraph 5 of Article II of the Treaty shall not affect
                    generally recognized principles of international law relating to the passage of
                    submarines or flights of aircraft or relating to visits of submarines to ports
                    of States not party to this Treaty.</p>
                <p>The Parties further agree that, with regard to heavy bombers, paragraph 5 of
                    Article II of the Treaty shall not preclude the temporary stationing for
                    extended periods of time of heavy bombers outside the national territory of a
                    Party. If a Party stations heavy bombers outside its national territory for a
                    period in excess of 30 days at any one time, it shall advise the other Party
                    through diplomatic channels before the end of the 30-day period.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
